<title>Callisto Workspace Audit</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #f4f5f3;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --surface-2: #ebecea;
    --border: #d8dad5;
    --text: #1b1e1c;
    --text-muted: #5a5f5a;
    --text-faint: #8a8f89;
    --accent: #1f7a72;
    --accent-soft: #e4f1ef;
    --link: #16645d;
    --crit-fg: #a3121a;
    --crit-bg: #fbe4e4;
    --crit-border: #e8a6a6;
    --high-fg: #9a5300;
    --high-bg: #fdecd2;
    --high-border: #edc182;
    --med-fg: #7a6400;
    --med-bg: #f8f0cf;
    --med-border: #ddca7e;
    --low-fg: #1f5a8a;
    --low-bg: #e2edf7;
    --low-border: #a9c8e0;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20,20,15,0.04), 0 4px 14px rgba(20,20,15,0.05);
    --serif: ui-serif, Georgia, "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", "Times New Roman", serif;
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", "Cascadia Code", "Roboto Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg: #14161a;
    --surface: #1b1e23;
    --surface-2: #22262c;
    --border: #30353c;
    --text: #e7e8e6;
    --text-muted: #a2a7ac;
    --text-faint: #6d7278;
    --accent: #5fc4ba;
    --accent-soft: #1c3532;
    --link: #7ad4ca;
    --crit-fg: #ff8f8f;
    --crit-bg: #3a1c1e;
    --crit-border: #6b2c2e;
    --high-fg: #ffbf6b;
    --high-bg: #3a2b14;
    --high-border: #6b4a1e;
    --med-fg: #eddb7a;
    --med-bg: #35300f;
    --med-border: #62551d;
    --low-fg: #8fc3ee;
    --low-bg: #17293a;
    --low-border: #2b4b68;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
  }

  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #14161a;
      --surface: #1b1e23;
      --surface-2: #22262c;
      --border: #30353c;
      --text: #e7e8e6;
      --text-muted: #a2a7ac;
      --text-faint: #6d7278;
      --accent: #5fc4ba;
      --accent-soft: #1c3532;
      --link: #7ad4ca;
      --crit-fg: #ff8f8f;
      --crit-bg: #3a1c1e;
      --crit-border: #6b2c2e;
      --high-fg: #ffbf6b;
      --high-bg: #3a2b14;
      --high-border: #6b4a1e;
      --med-fg: #eddb7a;
      --med-bg: #35300f;
      --med-border: #62551d;
      --low-fg: #8fc3ee;
      --low-bg: #17293a;
      --low-border: #2b4b68;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.3), 0 6px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
    }
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  ::selection { background: var(--accent-soft); }

  a { color: var(--link); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:focus-visible, button:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  code, .path {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: var(--surface-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    color: var(--text);
    word-break: break-word;
  }

  .layout {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 48px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 920px) {
    .layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .toc-wrap { display: none; }
  }

  header.masthead {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 56px 24px 40px;
  }
  .masthead-inner { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.7rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    text-wrap: balance;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .scope-line {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
    margin: 0 0 28px;
  }

  .stat-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 9px 14px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .stat b { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 1.15rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .stat span { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .stat.crit b { color: var(--crit-fg); }
  .stat.high b { color: var(--high-fg); }
  .stat.med b { color: var(--med-fg); }
  .stat.low b { color: var(--low-fg); }

  .toc-wrap { padding-top: 48px; }
  nav.toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: 24px;
  }
  nav.toc .toc-title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.74rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  nav.toc ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  nav.toc li a {
    display: block;
    padding: 5px 0 5px 14px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.89rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
    margin-left: -1px;
  }
  nav.toc li a:hover { color: var(--text); border-left-color: var(--text-faint); }
  nav.toc li.sub a { padding-left: 26px; font-size: 0.83rem; }

  main { padding: 48px 0 96px; min-width: 0; }

  section { margin-bottom: 56px; scroll-margin-top: 20px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    scroll-margin-top: 20px;
  }
  h3.theme-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.22rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 40px 0 18px;
    scroll-margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  h3.theme-title:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }

  p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  strong { font-weight: 650; }

  .callout {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    margin: 20px 0;
  }
  ol.top-actions { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
  ol.top-actions li { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  ol.top-actions li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .finding {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 20px 24px 22px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .finding-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 10px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .pill {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    border: 1px solid;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .pill.crit { color: var(--crit-fg); background: var(--crit-bg); border-color: var(--crit-border); }
  .pill.high { color: var(--high-fg); background: var(--high-bg); border-color: var(--high-border); }
  .pill.med  { color: var(--med-fg);  background: var(--med-bg);  border-color: var(--med-border); }
  .pill.low  { color: var(--low-fg);  background: var(--low-bg);  border-color: var(--low-border); }
  .finding-title {
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .unverified-tag {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    border: 1px dashed var(--border);
    border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    white-space: nowrap;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .finding .locpath { margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .finding .locpath code { font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .finding .body p { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .finding .body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .finding .label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-right: 6px;
  }
  .verified-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-top: 10px;
  }

  .flat-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; }
  .flat-list li { margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .flat-list li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  footer {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 28px 24px 60px;
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  footer .inner { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
  }
</style>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="masthead-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">Adversarial multi-agent audit &middot; 10-crate Cargo + Moon workspace</p>
    <h1>Callisto Workspace Audit</h1>
    <p class="scope-line">Architecture, domain modeling, correctness, security, performance, dependency hygiene, test coverage, and documentation &mdash; reviewed by 8 parallel finder agents, then adversarially re-verified before synthesis. Three Critical findings were independently reproduced by hand, one with a compiled repro against this workspace's real dependencies.</p>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat crit"><b>3</b><span>critical</span></div>
      <div class="stat high"><b>7</b><span>high</span></div>
      <div class="stat med"><b>25</b><span>medium</span></div>
      <div class="stat low"><b>16</b><span>low</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="layout">
  <div class="toc-wrap">
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p class="toc-title">Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#summary">Executive Summary</a></li>
        <li><a href="#findings">Findings by Theme</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-architecture">Architecture &amp; Layering</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-modeling">Domain Modeling &amp; Seams</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-bugs">Correctness / Bugs</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-security">Security</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-performance">Performance</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-deps">Dependency &amp; Crate Usage</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-tests">Test Coverage</a></li>
        <li class="sub"><a href="#t-docs">Documentation &amp; Organization</a></li>
        <li><a href="#crates">Crates to Adopt / Use Better</a></li>
        <li><a href="#reorganize">Reorganize / Test / Document</a></li>
        <li><a href="#actions">Prioritized Action List</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <main>

    <section id="summary">
      <h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Callisto is a mature, disciplined codebase &mdash; strict layering, <code>unsafe_code = "forbid"</code> everywhere, format-preserving CST editors instead of regex hacks, atomic-write-with-fsync persistence, and a CI gate (<code>just ci</code>) that actually enforces zero clippy warnings and full E2E coverage. Most of what this audit surfaces is exactly what you'd expect from a fast-moving session on top of a solid base: a handful of real correctness/security bugs in brand-new code (the publish pipeline hardening and the new <code>matrix.rs</code>/<code>config/pattern.rs</code> modules), a long tail of documentation drift, and dependency hygiene that has slipped slightly out of sync with the workspace's own stated policy. There is no evidence of systemic architectural rot &mdash; the layer boundaries hold, the AGPL/permissive split is intentional (if inconsistently labeled in docs), and the confirmed bugs are concentrated in exactly the areas the audit was told to focus on: <code>publish_client.rs</code>, the new <code>matrix.rs</code>/<code>pattern.rs</code> modules, and the CLI publish/status wiring.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <p style="margin-bottom:12px;"><strong>The five things worth acting on first:</strong></p>
        <ol class="top-actions">
          <li><strong>The version-inheritance parser bug is a self-inflicted outage.</strong> <code>cargo_publish</code>'s pre-publish version guard cannot parse <code>version.workspace = true</code> &mdash; the exact pattern all 10 of this repo's own crates use. Right now, running <code>callisto publish</code> on itself would hard-fail on every crate. Same-day fix and regression test.</li>
          <li><strong><code>PublishTarget::NuGet</code>/<code>GitHubRelease</code> are accepted but never wired to a publisher</strong>, and the release-tag gate doesn't check whether anything was actually published. A config typo can produce a git tag and a <code>ReleaseEntry</code> claiming a release happened when nothing was pushed to any registry &mdash; the highest-consequence bug in the batch, precisely because it fails silently.</li>
          <li><strong>Two real path-traversal / SSRF holes</strong> reachable from config or manifest files that get normal PR review but no automated containment check &mdash; an absolute or <code>..</code>-laden <code>changelog</code>/<code>changesets.dir</code> value can write or read outside the workspace root on CI, and an npm package's own <code>publishConfig.registry</code> field can redirect <code>npm publish</code>/<code>npm view</code> to an arbitrary host while <code>NPM_TOKEN</code> is in the environment. Both are cheap to fix with one shared path-containment helper and one registry allowlist check.</li>
          <li><strong>The <code>[[package-set]]</code> ecosystem-prefix feature is dead on arrival</strong> &mdash; and three separate audit passes independently rediscovered the same bug from three different angles, a strong signal it's real.</li>
          <li><strong>Documentation drift is real but not urgent</strong>: <code>callisto matrix</code> (a ~1,000-line flagship feature shipped this session) is entirely absent from <code>docs/00-design.md</code> and nearly absent from <code>docs/01-spec.md</code>; <code>callisto-vcs</code> has no crate-letter section at all.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p><strong>Calibration:</strong> nothing here should be read as "this codebase is in trouble." The confirmed-critical findings are narrow, mechanical, and fast to fix (parser edge case, missing exhaustiveness check, missing path containment). The bulk of the 41 unverified findings are legitimate but low-stakes &mdash; undocumented traits, redundant git discoveries that cost milliseconds, unused dependencies. Treat the confirmed bucket as a punch list for this week; treat the unverified bucket as a backlog to burn down opportunistically, prioritizing the ones that touch the freshly-written publish/matrix/pattern surface over the long-stable Layer 1/2 crates.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

