```

`&dyn CommitWalker` rather than a generic parameter is a deliberate, compatible choice: §M.10
keeps the trait dyn-compatible precisely so that any `&GitAccess`/`&GitRepository`/`&ShellGit`
(all three implement `CommitWalker`, §V.7) coerces here with no adapter. Neither form is
privileged. Note there is no `cwd: &Path` parameter here — unlike the `CommandRunner`-based
functions elsewhere in this crate (§C.6), a `CommitWalker` implementation already carries its
own repository root internally (e.g. `GitAccess::discover`'s `root`), so this function has no
separate root to be told.

